      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "I'll read both the original test and the CUT source to understand the code before improving it.Now I understand the test. It verifies that `CharRange.isNotIn` auto-reverses arguments when they are passed in reversed order (`'e', 'a'` → stored as `'a'`–`'e'`). I'll improve understandability by adding a clear naming convention, inline comments that explain the *why*, and a descriptive display name.Let me check where `compile.sh` expects the test file.The file needs to be in the working directory. I wrote it to the wrong path — let me fix that.The improved test compiles successfully. The refactoring adds a class-level Javadoc explaining the key auto-reversal behaviour being tested, renames the local variable to `reversedNegatedRange` to make its role immediately obvious, and attaches a short failure message to each assertion so a reader knows *why* each property is expected — without changing any method calls, arguments, or expected values."
